# taptest: the frame stream with no continuous input, and one 0.5 s single-finger tap partway in.
#
# The question is whether a touch changes a state that stops the frames, or whether only sustained
# high-rate input costs the frames. One tap and nothing after it tells the two apart: a dip that
# never recovers means the state changed; a dip that recovers, or no dip at all, means the input
# itself is not what stops the stream.
#
# The tap comes at wait 40 rather than later because the measured frame stream starts within a few
# seconds of the job and lasts 25 to 90 s; a later tap can fall after the stream has stopped, which
# is the one place this probe cannot answer anything.
/redwood/bin/lsprobe 60 &
/redwood/bin/lsprobe 300 &
/redwood/bin/framewatch --every 20 --count 30 SpringBoard backboardd &
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 40 tap 0.5 0.5 wait 260
